# Project governance

- Respect the approved architecture (Flutter mobile, Next.js web/admin, NestJS modular monolith API, worker, PostgreSQL/Supabase, OpenAPI, outbox notifications).
- Analysis is closed; do not reinterpret the baseline to expand scope.
- No unapproved scope changes — post-baseline work requires a Change Request.
- Do not write to `main` directly.
- Do not create commits or push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not initialize application frameworks or install dependencies unless the task explicitly requires it.
- Prefer repository foundation and documentation changes over speculative feature code when scope is foundation-only.
